body:
Controller logs showed the safety-retract command `G53 G1 Z0.000 F12000` returning `error:9` after a probe alarm, while the machine sat at `WPos:304.799,138.109,-102.080`. On GrblHAL, a probe alarm clears the homed flag — G53 is then rejected with error:9, but the ncSender API still returns HTTP 200, making the failure completely silent. The app then issued `G90 G1 X0.000 Y0.000` with Z still at −102 mm.

## Root cause
`G53` requires the machine to be homed. After probe alarm → `$X` unlock, `homed` is `false` (or unknown). All three G53 retract paths (`stopNowAndSafeHome`, `retrySafetyMoves`, `_outlineSafetyRetract`) issued G53 unconditionally.

## Changes

- **`stopNowAndSafeHome` (core.js)** — Fetches machine state and calls `_detectHomed()` before the retract block. Uses G53 only when `homed === true`; falls back to `G91 G1 Z10` + `G90` otherwise. Logs the decision.

- **`retrySafetyMoves` (core.js)** — Same guard, reusing the state object already fetched for the alarm/hold pre-check. Logs `pre-retract homed=...` and the reason for skipping G53.

  ```js
  // Before (always used G53 when machineSafeTopZ was configured):
  if (_retryMachineSafeZ !== null) {
    await sendCommand('G53 G1 Z' + _retryMachineSafeZ.toFixed(3) + ' F' + retractFeed.toFixed(0));
  }

  // After (guards on confirmed homed state):
  if (_retryMachineSafeZ !== null && _retryHomed === true) {
    await sendCommand('G53 G1 Z' + _retryMachineSafeZ.toFixed(3) + ' F' + retractFeed.toFixed(0));
  } else {
    // relative lift — safe without re-homing
    await sendCommand('G91 G1 Z10 F' + retractFeed.toFixed(0));
    ...
    await sendCommand('G90');
  }
  ```

- **`sendUnlockCommand` (core.js)** — After polling to Idle post-`$X`, calls `getMachineSnapshot()` and logs the real `WPos` and `homed` state before safety moves run. Previously the position display stayed at stale `0,0,0` through the entire recovery flow.

- **`_outlineSafetyRetract` (outline-probe.js)** — Checks `homed === true` before calling `moveMachineZAbs(0)`. Falls back to relative 10 mm lift when not homed. Logs `homed=` and current position at the start of every retract.

- **`moveMachineZAbs` (core.js)** — Added comment documenting the G53/homing requirement and the error:9 silent-failure risk for future callers.

## Summary

Operator discovered a friend's account had \`onboarding.complete=true\` with \`phoneVerified=false\`. Two related fixes close every remaining bypass.

### 1. DELETE \`POST /api/onboarding/skip\`

The route silently set \`onboarding.complete=true\` without phone verification. Zero UI references (grep confirmed), but a technical user could hit it directly via DevTools fetch / curl / Postman. Replaced with a tombstone comment.

### 2. Add \`requirePhoneVerified\` to \`POST /api/bids/:leadId/buy-now\`

Dashboard buy-now was the only purchase path without a phoneVerified gate. Now joins activation pay, top-up, SMS Claim opt-in, onboarding/complete, and onboarding step >=4. SMS Claim purchase (twilio.js) was already gated by an inline check.

### 3. Update middleware docstring

Lists every chokepoint + records the \`/skip\` deletion so the next audit reads the complete picture from the middleware header.

## Tests (8 source-pin cases, all green)

| # | Pins |
|---|---|
| S1 | onboarding.js no longer registers POST /skip |
| S2 | No handler still sets onboarding.complete via skip-like route |
| S3 | Tombstone comment present |
| B1 | bids.js imports requirePhoneVerified |
| B2 | POST /:leadId/buy-now has auth + requirePhoneVerified |
| B3 | POST /:leadId/settle does NOT mount requirePhoneVerified (cron-only) |
| M1 | Middleware docstring lists bids.js buy-now |
| M2 | Middleware docstring records /skip deletion |

## Verification

- 1341/1341 server tests pass
- Client build clean

## Operator follow-up (Mongo, not shipped here)

\`\`\`js
// Count affected accounts
db.users.countDocuments({
  'onboarding.complete': true,
  phoneVerified: { \$ne: true }
});

// List them with detail for triage
db.users.find({
  'onboarding.complete': true,
  phoneVerified: { \$ne: true }
}, {
  email: 1, phone: 1, phoneVerified: 1,
  onboarding: 1, createdAt: 1, balance: 1
});

// Reset onboarding for zero-balance affected accounts
db.users.updateMany({
  'onboarding.complete': true,
  phoneVerified: { \$ne: true },
  balance: { \$lte: 0 }
}, {
  \$set: {
    'onboarding.complete': false,
    'onboarding.needsPhoneVerification': true
  },
  \$unset: {
    'onboarding.completedAt': '',
    'onboarding.skippedAt': ''
  }
});
\`\`\`

